nventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIDA, NAOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NODA, KOUTA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEGAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHOUDA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKADA, KIYOTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An opening is made in a resin (20) with a laser to form a viahole. A copper foil (22) etched into a thin film (3  mu m) to lower the heat conductivity is used as a conformal mask, thereby making an opening (20a) in the resin (20) by fewer times of irradiation with a pulse laser beam. This prevents formation of any undercut in the resin (20) on which an interlayer resin-insulating layer is to be formed, enabling improvement in the connection reliability of the viahole.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On pratique un trou dans une résine (20) avec un laser pour former un trou d'interconnexion. Une feuille (22) de cuivre gravée dans un film mince (3  mu m) pour réduire la conductivité thermique sert de masque conforme, ce qui permet de pratiquer une ouverture (20a) dans la résine (20) avec un temps moindre d'irradiation au moyen d'un faisceau laser pulsé. Cette technique empêche la formation d'une attaque latérale dans la résine (20) sur laquelle on doit former une couche intermédiaire, ce qui permet d'améliorer la fiabilité de connexion du trou d'interconnexion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>